{"updated":"2026-11-07T11:40:40Z","categories":{"cloud":"Cloud","dev":"Development","network":"Network & CDN","collab":"Collaboration","ai":"AI"},"summary":{"total":27,"failing":5,"worst":"major","no_data":0},"providers":[{"id":"aws","name":"AWS","category":"cloud","web":"https://health.aws.amazon.com/health/status","status":"partial","description":"","components":[{"name":"Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Oregon)","status":"partial"},{"name":"Multiple services (UAE)","status":"partial"},{"name":"Multiple services (Bahrain)","status":"partial"}],"total_components":0,"affected":3,"limited_scope":false,"incidents":[{"id":"arn:aws:health:us-west-2::event/EC2/AWS_EC2_OPERATIONAL_ISSUE/AWS_EC2_OPERATIONAL_ISSUE_62978_C9C1126888D","title":"Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Oregon): [RESOLVED] Elevated Launch Failures","impact":"partial","phase":"","started":"2026-11-06T22:51:05Z","updated":"2026-11-07T01:12:16Z","message":"Between 2:35 PM and 4:21 PM PST, we experienced elevated EC2 instance launch failures affecting all AZs (usw2-az1, usw2-az2, usw2-az3, usw2-az4) in the US-WEST-2 Region. EC2 Instance Launches, AWS services that instantiated new instances, as well as services such as DataSync or AWS Backup which require new instances to support data transfers to or from the US-WEST-2 Region were affected. Our engineers were automatically engaged and immediately began investigating the root cause. We identified the issue to be caused by a subsystem that supports EBS Volumes required during instance launch. We b…","link":"https://health.aws.amazon.com/health/status"},{"id":"arn:aws:health:me-central-1::event/MULTIPLE_SERVICES/AWS_MULTIPLE_SERVICES_OPERATIONAL_ISSUE/AWS_MULTIPLE_SERVICES_OPERATIONAL_ISSUE_5E6B8_EF2498889B5","title":"Multiple services (UAE): Region Availability","impact":"partial","phase":"","started":"2026-03-01T12:51:25Z","updated":"2026-09-15T10:27:10Z","message":"We are providing an update on the disruption affecting the Middle East (UAE) (me-central-1) Region.